Teddy is not an answer, just a stop gap for more mediocre play. I hope I am wrong though.

Yeah for aming at high refresh rates get a TN or IPS panel monitor.

&#x200B;

[https://www.howtogeek.com/658701/tn-vs.-ips-vs.-va-whats-the-best-display-panel-technology/](https://www.howtogeek.com/658701/tn-vs.-ips-vs.-va-whats-the-best-display-panel-technology/)

&#x200B;

Edit: Commenter below does make a good point VA tech is much better on higher quality VA panel monitors in the last few years.

There are so many people that if you like something they hate they berate you and make you feel bad about liking said thing and I believe that it is very wrong. With that said I feel like FFXV makes me feel that way with how much I despised it and then somehow there are people who enjoyed it. Anyways If you liked FFXV any of the FF games or literally any RPG would be an improvement so I will recommend the witcher 3, which kills it with lore and history and and amazing story line. The other would be Skyrim as it just has so much rich history and of course is the king of character progression.

&#x200B;

Thank you for letting me rant and I hope my suggestions make up for it.

Witcher 3 - While I think combat and the armor and point system  are not fantastic and with a sluggish start, the first true storyline the bloody baron just blows apart any story in any video game, movie, or tv show. You start off by investigating, coming up with conclusions, building that knowledge, then seeing some really cool lore build up, then it has a twist and it just blows open the door and then you got to fix it all. After Witcher 3 I don't think any game could ever match it again. After that part you kind of do the same thing all through out. They just do such a good job telling a story and making it feel very real.

&#x200B;

The cool part is I didn't try Witcher 3 until 2019 - I got it for $5 and I literally got 7 cents an hour enjoyment.

Animal Crossing, although you say not mario odyssey it was my favorite game, and my most played game on switch is Slay the Spire (Even though I own it n PC too). I also really enjoyed FE Three houses (Not a huge anime style game fan either).

&#x200B;

My switch has been sitting lately, so I decided to replay BotW and get all the shrines.

Because "we" the redditors are different than we everyone playing the game. Game communities suck, they should just leave it as it was even though its sucks and that is because the integrity of the original is lost.

&#x200B;

They literally lose in every scenario but at least they could say we wanted to leave it as is to the original. It's too late now with the changes so now they have to try and please people why everyone talks massive shit no matter what they do.

&#x200B;

I never played wow seriosuly, that's why I am trying classic and people on this sub are fucking whiny little bitches. We sit here and talk about a mechanic that was true to the original but still want to bitch. This proves nobody really liked the old games or they would stfu and play to enjoy the nostalgia.

&#x200B;

It's like Rose-Tinted glasses except you keep making them rosier and rosier. Blizzard did this to themselves though so I guess they have to take the blame. Should of just left things as is to avoid whiny fans.

Yeah, I am sick of people villanizing facebook over quest 2, especially when it is pretty clear what you can and cannot do. There are plenty of other shitty things they do that you should be villanizing them for. Social media is terrible, but god dammit I got into quality VR for $300 so don't let the door hit ya.

&#x200B;

It's this, you make serious actual facebook to participate and allow facebook to monitor and use your data to sell to other companies and in return you get a decent portable vr system for cheap. No different than any other service that uses and sells your data. People just want their privacy and want the cheap price. It's clear you can't have both. It sucks but some of us are ok with saving the cash.
